<title>USA: High Plains Wheat - Basis strengthens, sales slow.</title>
<headline>High Plains Wheat - Basis strengthens, sales slow.</headline>
<dateline>KANSAS CITY, Mo. 1997-05-06</dateline>
<text>
<p>Hard red winter wheat basis bids strengthened at many locations on Tuesday with farmer old crop sales at a virtual standstill.</p>
<p>Dealers said farmers in much of Kansas were preoccupied with corn planting. The weekly state crop report, issued Monday, reported that 50 percent of Kansas corn had been planted and sorghum and soybean seeding had just begun.</p>
<p>&quot;There is nothing going on. The farmers are in the fields,&quot; one Kansas dealer said.</p>
<p>Dealers also noted that little old crop wheat remained unsold.  </p>
